dtk-update (0.0.2) beige; urgency=medium

  * feat: scheduled update check (disabled/hour/day/month) with live hot-reload of
    schedule; configurable from dde-dock tray menu, generic tray submenu and main GUI.
  * feat: opt-in automatic update (default off); only periodic-check discovered
    updates auto-install, security advisory / pre-check still require explicit confirm
    (default focus cancel); manual/event-triggered checks never auto-update.
  * fix: DConfig boolean switches were silently ineffective (schema keys are camelCase,
    read via wrong lower-case key) — now mapped through explicit PascalCase→camelCase
    table, locked by regression test.
  * fix: manual/UI triggered updates bypassed confirm dialog when advisory hidden — now
    always prompt (cancel-focused).
  * fix: post-update cleanup callback mis-identification after cancel (stale callbacks
    could falsely report completion) — guarded by in-flight cleanup count + orphan
    callback guard.
  * fix: orphan autoremove now only runs when a system backend actually upgraded this
    round (no autoremove on sandbox-only upgrades).
  * fix: generic tray double-free on destroy; daemon duplicate login1/NetworkManager
    signal subscription; stray autostart desktop file launching GUI on boot.
  * fix: openSUSE candidate version mis-map (zypper list-updates header); GUI version
    hardcoded 0.1.0 corrected to 0.0.2.
  * fix: generic tray menu memory leak (unparented QMenu); translations sourcelanguage
    rewrite bug; empty/zero-target write ops now always return a result.
  * feat(pacman): implement checkConfigFilesToReview (.pacnew/.pacsave/.pacorig) scan
    under /etc via QDirIterator, locked by regression test.
  * ci: dde-tray build is now distro-aware — deepin/UOS requires dde-tray-loader-dev and
    verifies pluginsiteminterface.h (hard fail CI), non-deepin skips gracefully.
  * docs: AGENTS.md updated skills list + new code-quality gating section.

 -- dtk-update maintainers <maintainer@dtk-update.local>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dtk-update (0.0.1) beige; urgency=medium

  * Initial stable release.
  * Distribution-agnostic DTK tray applet for package update management, with a
    pluggable backend abstraction over apt/dpkg, dnf/rpm, pacman, zypper and the
    sandboxed app ecosystems (linyaps/linglong, snap, flatpak).
  * Two tray integrations: native dde-dock plugin (Deepin/UOS, via
    dde-tray-loader PluginsItemInterfaceV2) and a generic freedesktop
    QSystemTrayIcon (no dde-dock dependency); plus a standalone GUI and an
    optional D-Bus/systemd user daemon.
  * Pre-update / post-update health checks (reboot-required, services-needing-
    restart, config-files-to-review, failed systemd units) — read-only probes,
    container-aware, never auto-applies.
  * Per-distribution upstream security advisories (Debian DSA / Ubuntu USN /
    openSUSE / Arch) with asynchronous prefetch and graceful timeout fallback;
    optional per-distro "recent news/notices" fetching.
  * Dependency resolution from backend dry-run output; residual package and
    download-cache reporting for explicit user cleanup.
  * Process-level concurrency lock (QLockFile) prevents concurrent GUI/tray
    system writes; all privileged writes go through pkexec/polkit.
  * Transparent configuration via DConfig + user-editable backend.conf;
    five-language localization (zh_CN/en_US/es/fr/de).
  * Multi-architecture deb packaging (amd64/arm64/loong64) via debootstrap deepin
    beige chroot + qemu; GitHub Actions build/test/lint pipelines.

 -- dtk-update taotieren <admin@taotieren.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
